━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Comprehensions is facet of FunctionEmitter
    sees Calls
    sees Lazies
    sees LiveActions
    sees Loops
    sees Streams

────────────────────
_ do emit-broadcaster Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId

` A comprehension on a stream where it is written: the container is made a `Broadcastable`,
` the channel is made and kept in the local the subscriber captures, and the subscriber, the
` environment in force here, is made a `Subscriber` and given to the broadcaster's
` `subscribe`, whose errors leave the function as the type pass said, or subscribed as
` `subscribe-whenever` says where the comprehension has a `whenever` clause. The channel, read again
` from where it is kept, is the comprehension's value. One written in the value of a global,
` where the function that types the value is not the one emitted, keeps the channel in an
` environment of its own: see `lone-environment`. One that is the value of a lazy local nested
` functions capture, evaluated by a function written in the one that declares the local, keeps
` it in the environment that holds the local, as `emit-closure` gives that environment.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. stream = emit-broadcastable(loop, container)
. broadcaster = stream.type
. made = call-at(id, .call-constructor)
. slot = channel-slot(id)
. channel = facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
. closure = subscriber-closure(id)
if made == no-fact || slot == no-slot || closure == no-type || other-channel
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. other-channel = instances.signatures[facts.calls[made].callee].returns != channel
. lone = if unit.reading != unit.instance && shared-written(id) == no-slot then lone-environment(id, slot) else no-local
. object = call-instance(facts.calls[made].callee, id, pending.length)
. written = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if lone == no-local
    keep-captured(slot, object.operand, channel, id)
    written = emit-closure(id, closure)
else
    keep-lone(lone, slot, object.operand, channel, id)
    written = Typed(load-local(lone, id), closure)
. subscriber = convert(id, .reason-argument, written)
. given = subscriber.type
. owned = tables.owned-subscription-of(unit.reading, id)
. retested = tree.whenever-clause(loop)
. retest = tables.live-statement-of(unit.reading, retested) if retested != 0
if retest
    subscribe-whenever(id, retested, retest, stream.operand, broadcaster, subscriber.operand)
else if retested != 0
    refuse(.refused-expression, retested)
else if owned
    own-subscription(id, owned, stream.operand, subscriber.operand)
else
    do call-protocol(id, call-at(id, .call-method), stream.operand, broadcaster, subscriber.operand, given)
if lone != no-local
    = Typed(take(load-local(lone, id), lone-field(slot), id), channel)
= read-captured(slot, id, channel)

────────────────────
+ do emit-comprehension Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - loop SyntaxId

` A comprehension written as a value: a call of the function generated for it. The
` container of its loop is evaluated here, where the comprehension is written, and given
` to the function. The call gives the generator. One on a stream subscribes here instead:
` see `emit-broadcaster`.
. container SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[loop]
    | .node-loop-syntax(row)
        if row.is-subscriber
            = emit-broadcaster(id, loop, row.container)
        container = row.container
if container == 0
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
= emit-comprehension-call(id, container)

────────────────────
_ do emit-comprehension-call Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId
    - converts Bool = false

` The call of the function generated for a comprehension, or for a stream piped through a
` pattern, given the container, which gives the generator. A container that `converts` is
` converted as the type pass recorded for it as an argument.
. answer = call-generated(id, container, converts)
if answer.type != facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
= answer

────────────────────
_ do call-generated Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - given-site SyntaxId
    - converts Bool = false

` A call of the function generated for what is written at a node, a comprehension, a list
` of feeds or the right side of a pipe, which the type pass recorded there. It is given
` the environment in force, which the function reads the locals it captures from, and
` then the value written at `given-site`, where it takes one, evaluated here, and where it
` `converts`, converted as the type pass recorded for it as an argument. One written in
` the value a class writes for a property is typed by the instance that types that value,
` and given no environment, where that instance makes none: it captures nothing. Where it
` makes one it has no shape. One written in the value of a lazy local nested functions
` capture, evaluated by a function written in the one that declares it (`read-shared`), is
` given the environment that holds the local, which is the one in force where it is written.
` One a constructor makes has no shape where `emit-closure` gives a nested function none: while
` the properties are given their values, where nested functions read the receiver, and after,
` where the properties read a lazy local nested functions capture.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. callee = no-instance
. propagates = false
. fact = facts.first-call(unit.reading, id)
while fact != no-fact
    if facts.calls[fact].form == .call-closure
        callee = facts.calls[fact].callee
        propagates = facts.calls[fact].propagates
    fact = facts.calls[fact].next
. count U32 = if given-site != 0 then 1 else 0
. outside = unit.reading != unit.instance
. held = outside && tables.environments[unit.reading] != no-layout
. shared = shared-slot()
. receiving = filling.storing && !outside && shares-receiver()
. doubled = !filling.storing && !outside && fills-share() && shares-lazy()
if callee == no-instance || (held && shared == no-slot) || receiving || doubled
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if outside && instances.rows[callee].enclosing != unit.reading
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if tables.instance-functions[callee] == no-function || other-arity
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. other-arity = instances.signatures[callee].args.count != count
. given-value = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if given-site != 0
    given-value = emit-expression(given-site)
    if converts
        given-value = convert(given-site, .reason-argument, given-value)
    if given-value.type != instances.argument-type(callee, 0)
        refuse(.refused-conversion, given-site)
. written = nested-environment(id)
if outside && tables.stack-holds(callee).length != 0
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
hold-stacks(id, instances.rows[callee].decl, written)
. mark = pending.length
pending += written
if given-site != 0
    pending += given-value.operand
. raising = instances.signatures[callee].errors.count != 0
takes-result = raising
. answer = call-instance(callee, id, mark)
takes-result = false
=? propagate(id, callee, answer.operand) if raising && propagates
= answer

────────────────────
+ do emit-feed-list Typed
    - id SyntaxId

` A list of feeds written as a value: a call of the function generated for it, which the
` type pass recorded at the first feed, and which gives the generator.
= call-generated(id, 0)

────────────────────
+ do emit-feeds
    - first SyntaxId

` The body of the function generated for a list of feeds: each feed in turn yields
` its item, converted as the type pass recorded for the list at the item; one written
` `*?` yields what an optional holds, where it holds anything; and one written `**`
` yields every item of what it writes, by the loop the type pass planned at the feed.
` An item written as a cast keeps the cast's conversion where the list's is kept, so only
` the conversions of what the item gave are made. One written `*?` whose item is no
` optional has no shape yet.
. feed = first
while feed != 0
    . next SyntaxId = 0
    do match? tree.nodes[feed]
        | .node-feed-expression(row)
            next = row.next
            if row.is-spread
                emit-spread(feed, row.item, row.is-optional)
            else
                . value = convert-matched
                    - row.item
                    - .reason-explicit
                    - emit-expression(row.item)
                    - no-type
                if row.is-optional && !types.is-optional(value.type)
                    refuse(.refused-expression, feed)
                yield-item(facts.feed-site(unit.reading, feed), value, row.is-optional)
    feed = next

────────────────────
+ do emit-built-feeds
    - declared SyntaxId
    - first SyntaxId

. list = build-feeds(first, first, returns-type, .reason-return)
return-value(list.operand, declared)

────────────────────
+ do emit-listed-feeds Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - first SyntaxId

= build-feeds(id, first, facts.node-type(unit.reading, id), .reason-element)

────────────────────
_ do build-feeds Typed ?! Refused
    - home SyntaxId
    - first SyntaxId
    - listed TypeId
    - reason ConversionReason

. appends = call-at(home, .call-list-append)
if appends == no-fact || first == 0
    refuse(.refused-expression, home)
    = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
. outer-list = built-list
. outer-item = built-item
. outer-append = built-append
. outer-reason = built-reason
. outer-spreading = spreading
built-append = facts.calls[appends].callee
built-item = instances.argument-type(built-append, 0)
built-reason = reason
spreading = 0
. count U32 = 0
. room U32 = 0
. leading = true
. feed = first
while feed != 0
    do match? tree.nodes[feed]
        | .node-feed-expression(row)
            leading = leading && !row.is-spread && !row.is-optional
            if leading
                count += 1
            else if !row.is-spread
                room += 1
    feed = tree.next-feed(feed)
. mark = open-cleanups.length
. own-scoping = scoping
scoping = scoping.block-base = mark
. start = given.length
feed = first
for _ in 0 .. < count
    do match? tree.nodes[feed]
        | .node-feed-expression(row)
            . value = convert-matched(row.item, .reason-explicit, emit-expression(row.item), no-type)
            . site = facts.feed-site(unit.reading, feed)
            . converted = built-value(site, value)
            if converted.type != built-item
                refuse(.refused-conversion, site)
            given += Typed(apart(converted, row.item, count > 1), converted.type)
    feed = tree.next-feed(feed)
. list = build-list(home, RowRange'SyntaxId(0, count), listed, start, false, first, room)
drop-given(start)
built-list = list.operand
while feed != 0
    do match? tree.nodes[feed]
        | .node-feed-expression(row)
            if row.is-spread
                spreading = feed
                emit-spread(feed, row.item, row.is-optional)
                spreading = 0
            else
                . value = convert-matched(row.item, .reason-explicit, emit-expression(row.item), no-type)
                if row.is-optional && !types.is-optional(value.type) && reason == .reason-return
                    refuse(.refused-expression, feed)
                append-built(facts.feed-site(unit.reading, feed), value, row.is-optional)
    feed = tree.next-feed(feed)
. built = close-value(list, mark, own-scoping, home)
built-list = outer-list
built-item = outer-item
built-append = outer-append
built-reason = outer-reason
spreading = outer-spreading
= built

────────────────────
_ do emit-spread
    - feed SyntaxId
    - item SyntaxId
    - optional Bool

` A spread of what it writes. Of a range of integers written there,
` the loop that counts through it. Of a container, a loop over it by the protocol the type
` pass planned at the feed, whose slots keep the container, converted first to the iterable
` it is read as where it is not one: `**?` reads what an optional holds and gives nothing
` where it holds none. Each item is yielded as it is read. What the
` loop does at the feed is located on the line under it where the type pass noted that.
. plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, feed)
if plan == .plan-range-loop && !optional
    do match? tree.nodes[item]
        | .node-range-expression(range)
            emit-range-loop(feed, range.op, range.left, range.right, 0, 0)
            =
if plan != .plan-index-loop && plan != .plan-cursor-loop && plan != .plan-stream-loop
    refuse(.refused-expression, feed)
    =
. slot = loop-slots(feed)
. held = convert(item, .reason-explicit, emit-expression(item))
. beyond = no-block
if optional && types.is-optional(held.type)
    . wrapped = held.type
    . given = ir.reserve-block()
    beyond = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(present(feed, held).operand, given, beyond)
    ir.start-block(given)
    held = payload(feed, Typed(held.operand, wrapped))
. site = facts.feed-site(unit.reading, feed)
if site != 0
    held = convert(site, .reason-operand, held)
keep-state(slot, held.operand, held.type, feed)
. shifted = lowered
lowered = if facts.is-feed-below(unit.reading, feed) then feed else 0
emit-headed(feed, item, 0, 0, true)
lowered = shifted
if beyond != no-block
    jump(beyond)
    ir.start-block(beyond)

────────────────────
+ do emit-pattern-pipe
    - pipe SyntaxId

` The body of the function generated for a stream piped through a pattern, as the reference makes
` it: the stream the pattern reads the value piped through is made, once, of what a feed the pipe
` reads alone writes where it reads one, evaluated then and converted as the type pass recorded.
` Then on each pass the stream releases what it delivered that no mark holds; it is asked whether
` it has more, and the function ends where it has not; its position is taken, and the pattern
` matched from where it is, as a rule's arms are, without reading the rest, asking the stream for
` more input where a part reads past the end of its buffer; the function ends where it fails. Where
` the match did not move the stream on, it panics; else what it gave is yielded. A helper the pipe
` is given is evaluated once, after the stream is made, and kept for every match to run under. One
` that marks the records a pipe matches is asked to begin each record, where the stream has more,
` before the stream's position is taken.
. right SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[pipe]
    | .node-pipeline-expression(row)
        right = row.right
    | .node-binary-expression(row)
        right = row.rhs
. pattern = right
. helper SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[right]
    | .node-stream-match(row)
        pattern = row.pattern
        helper = row.helper
. result = facts.node-type(unit.reading, pattern)
. first = facts.first-call(unit.reading, pipe)
. releases = if first != no-fact && facts.calls[first].form == .call-method then first else no-fact
. asks = if releases != no-fact then next-call(first) else first
. marks = next-call(asks)
. begins = next-call(marks)
if right == 0 || result == no-type || result == invalid-type || marks == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, pipe)
    =
. slot = loop-slots(pipe)
do match? tree.nodes[tree.piped-feed(pipe)]
    | .node-feed-expression(row)
        . written = convert(row.item, .reason-argument, emit-expression(row.item))
        keep-state(slot, written.operand, written.type, pipe)
. container = state(slot, pipe)
. container-type = container.type
. made = stream-maker(right)
. viewed = if made != no-fact then next-call(made) else facts.first-call(unit.reading, right)
. commits = next-call(viewed)
if commits == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, pipe)
    =
. opened = stream-of(right, container.operand, container-type, made)
keep-state(slot + 1, opened.operand, opened.type, pipe)
if helper != 0
    . helping = emit-expression(helper)
    keep-state(slot + 2, helping.operand, helping.type, pipe)
    if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, helper) != .plan-pattern-helper
        refuse(.refused-statement, pipe)
        =
. root = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
jump(root)
ir.start-block(root)
emit-poll(pipe)
. stream = state(slot + 1, pipe)
. stream-type = stream.type
if releases != no-fact
    call-protocol(pipe, releases, stream.operand, stream-type, make-operand(.operand-void, 0))
. more = call-protocol(pipe, asks, stream.operand, stream-type, make-operand(.operand-void, 0))
if more.type != types.bool-type
    refuse(.refused-statement, pipe)
    =
. moving = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(pipe, .compare-not-equal, more.operand, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), moving, done)
ir.start-block(moving)
if begins != no-fact
    . kept = state(slot + 2, pipe)
    call-protocol(pipe, begins, kept.operand, kept.type, make-operand(.operand-void, 0))
. began = marked-cursor(pipe, marks, stream.operand, stream-type)
. refills = made == no-fact || chunked
    .. chunked = same-decl(class-ref(types, stream-type), types.chunked-token-stream-decl)
. run = view-stream(right, stream.operand, stream-type, refills, viewed, next-call(commits))
if helper != 0
    . kept-state = state(slot + 2, pipe)
    streaming = streaming.pattern-helper = kept-state.operand
    streaming = streaming.pattern-helper-type = kept-state.type
. value = attempt-arms(right, pattern, result, run, false, commits, done, false)
. ended = marked-cursor(pipe, marks, stream.operand, stream-type)
. moved = ir.reserve-block()
. stuck = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(pipe, .compare-greater, ended.operand, began.operand), moved, stuck)
ir.start-block(stuck)
raise-text(right, "Grammar pipeline made no input progress")
ir.start-block(moved)
yield-item(right, Typed(value.operand, result), false)
jump(root)
ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
_ do marked-cursor Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - fact FactId
    - stream Operand
    - stream-type TypeId

` Where a stream is, as the mark the call the type pass recorded makes of it holds it.
. mark = call-protocol(site, fact, stream, stream-type, make-operand(.operand-void, 0))
. layout = layout-of(mark.type, site)
if !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout) || tables.layouts.rows[layout].fields.count != 2
    refuse(.refused-type, site)
    = mark
= part(mark.operand, layout, 1, site)

────────────────────
+ do keep-piped
    - declared SyntaxId

` Copies the item, or the value, a pipe gives the function generated for its right side into
` the function's environment, where nested functions capture its `each` or its `it`.
for offset in 0 .. < unit.slot-count
    . slot = unit.slot-start + offset
    . row = bindings.slots[slot]
    if (row.kind != .slot-each && row.kind != .slot-it) || row.syntax != piped || uncaptured
        continue
    .. uncaptured = !owns(slot) || !is-captured(slot)
    if ir.arguments.length != 2
        refuse(.refused-function, declared)
        =
    keep-captured
        - slot
        - make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
        - instances.argument-type(unit.instance, 0)
        - declared

────────────────────
_ do emit-stream-pipe Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - left SyntaxId

` A stream piped through a function over each of its items: the call the type pass
` recorded at the pipe, of the function of `core/stream` that maps, filters or taps a
` stream, given the stream on the left and the function generated for the right side as a
` value of the function type it takes.
` 1. The stream is evaluated, and converted as the type pass recorded where its facts are
`    kept: at the left side, or for a list of feeds at the feed after the first, or at
`    the pipe where there is none, for a reason of its own apart from the pipe's value.
` 2. The function is the environment its body is given (`nested-environment`), converted as
`    recorded at the pipe.
` A stack trace through the function on the right is the one TypeScript prints with no
` inlining. The answer has the type the function called returns: the type pass keeps the
` type of a list of one feed at the pipe that reads it.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fact = own-call(id)
. site = left
do match? tree.nodes[left]
    | .node-feed-expression(row)
        site = if row.next != 0 then row.next else id
. outside = unit.reading != unit.instance
if fact == no-fact || (holds-environment && shared-slot() == no-slot) || receiving
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. holds-environment = outside && tables.environments[unit.reading] != no-layout
.. receiving = filling.storing && !outside && shares-receiver()
. call = facts.calls[fact]
. callee = call.callee
if call.form != .call-function || callee == no-instance || call.is-partial || call.fills.count != 2
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. first = facts.call-fills[call.fills.start] as U32
. second = facts.call-fills[call.fills.start + 1] as U32
if first != 0 || second != 1 || tables.instance-functions[callee] == no-function
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. reason ConversionReason = if site == id then .reason-piped else .reason-argument
. source = convert-matched(site, reason, emit-expression(left), instances.argument-type(callee, 0))
if source.type != instances.argument-type(callee, 0)
    refuse(.refused-conversion, left)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. function = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. wanted = instances.argument-type(callee, 1)
. shape = facts.first-conversion(unit.reading, id)
while shape != no-fact && function.type != wanted
    . row = facts.conversions[shape]
    if row.reason == .reason-argument && is-closure(row.from) && row.runs != no-instance
        if outside && instances.rows[row.runs].enclosing != unit.reading
            refuse(.refused-expression, id)
            = Typed(nothing, no-type)
        function = convert-one(id, row, Typed(nested-environment(id), row.from))
    shape = row.next
if function.type != wanted
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. mark = pending.length
pending += source.operand
pending += function.operand
= call-instance(callee, id, mark)

────────────────────
_ do emit-write-all Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` A value written whole to what is on the right of the pipe: the one call the type pass
` recorded at the pipe, of the function the type on the right declares for a write, given
` the value. The value is evaluated first, as it is written first, and the pipe gives what
` it wrote to.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fact = facts.first-call(unit.reading, id)
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].next != no-fact || facts.calls[fact].is-swapped
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. made = emit-expression(left)
. value = apart(made, left, !is-inert(right))
. given = made.type
. sink = emit-expression(right)
. sink-type = sink.type
call-operator(id, fact, right, sink.operand, sink-type, left, value, given)
= Typed(sink.operand, sink-type)

────────────────────
_ do emit-write-each Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` Each item of what the pipe reads written to what is on the right, as the reference lowers
` it: what is on the right is evaluated first and kept, and the loop the type pass planned
` at the pipe reads the left, each turn giving the item to the write recorded at the pipe
` after the calls of the loop's protocol. A range of integers written there is counted
` through. The pipe gives what it wrote to.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fact = facts.first-call(unit.reading, id)
while fact != no-fact && facts.calls[fact].next != no-fact
    fact = facts.calls[fact].next
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].is-swapped
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. sink = emit-expression(right)
. sink-type = sink.type
. layout = layout-of(sink-type, id)
. kept = ir.add-local(layout)
store-local(kept, sink.operand, id)
writes += WriteEach(id, fact, left, right, kept, sink-type)
. plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, id)
. counted = false
do match? tree.nodes[left]
    | .node-range-expression(range)
        if plan == .plan-range-loop && range.left != 0 && range.right != 0
            emit-range-loop(id, range.op, range.left, range.right, 0, 0)
            counted = true
if !counted && (plan == .plan-index-loop || plan == .plan-cursor-loop || plan == .plan-stream-loop)
    emit-headed(id, left, 0, 0)
else if !counted
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
writes.pop()
. written = load-local(kept, id)
= Typed(written, sink-type)

────────────────────
_ do emit-piped Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - left SyntaxId

` A value given whole to the function generated for the right side of the pipe, which reads
` it as `it`: a call of that function, given the value.
. answer = call-generated(id, left)
if answer.type != facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
= answer

────────────────────
+ do emit-pipe Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` A value piped forward into the function written on the right, as the last argument of the
` call the type pass recorded at the pipe; a stream piped through the function written on
` the right, which maps, filters or taps its items, or through a pattern, as a comprehension
` is called, given what is piped as the type pass cast it, but for a feed that function
` evaluates; a value given whole to the function
` generated for the right side; or a value written whole, or each of its items, to what is
` on the right. Any other pipe has no shape yet. A list of feeds piped
` forward has what converts it kept at the feed after the first, beside what converts
` the yields of feeds, and a list of one feed at the pipe, apart from what converts the
` pipe's value.
if pipes-stream(op)
    = emit-stream-pipe(id, left)
if op == .grammar-pipe-op
    = emit-comprehension-call(id, if tree.piped-feed(id) == 0 then left else 0, true)
if op == .pipe-closure-op
    = emit-piped(id, left)
if op == .pipe-write-all-op
    = emit-write-all(id, left, right)
if op == .pipe-write-each-op
    = emit-write-each(id, left, right)
if op != .pipe-forward-op
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
=? emit-listed-feeds(id, tree.listed-feeds(id)) if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, id) == .plan-built-feeds
do match? tree.nodes[left]
    | .node-feed-expression(row)
        piped-site = if row.next != 0 then row.next else id
    | .node-pipeline-expression(row)
        if pipes-stream(row.op)
            piped-site = left
    | .node-binary-expression(row)
        if pipes-stream(row.op)
            piped-site = left
. answer = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
do match tree.nodes[right]
    | .node-call-expression(call)
        answer = emit-call-at(id, call.callable, call.args, left)
    ??
        answer = emit-call-at(id, right, RowRange'SyntaxId(), left)
piped-site = 0
= answer

────────────────────
_ do nested-environment Operand
    - id SyntaxId

` The environment a nested function of the instance whose facts are read is given where it is
` written: the one in force, or where a function written in that instance evaluates the value
` of a lazy local it declares, the one that holds the local, which is in force where the value
` is written (`shared-slot`). One made there by an instance with no environment is given none.
if unit.reading == unit.instance
    = written-environment(id)
. shared = shared-slot()
if shared == no-slot
    = integer(.machine-managed-pointer, 0)
find-captured(shared, id)
= captured-base(id)
